I was going to suggest almost exactly the same thing -- just a couple differences. Instead of this:

> # Take the twelve series and melt (or equivalently, stack) them:
> dm <- melt(d)
> # add an index variable:
> dm$index <- rep(1:32, 12)

Here is a slightly more general way of doing it:

# Add x values 1, 2, 3, ...
d$x <- 1:nrow(d)
# Convert to long format, keeping x as an identification var
dm <- melt(id.vars="x", d)

# With the expression, this works for me without needing the phantom 1:

ggplot(dm, aes(x = index, y = value/10000, group = variable)) + geom_line() +

   labs(x = "", y = expression(value %*% 10^4))

