Hi,

ggExtra was retired as it had become outdated and somewhat
incompatible with ggplot2. IIRC the fixedsize function stopped working
a long time ago, and even then it was just a hack. I've put the
original code here if you want to have a look
https://gist.github.com/1855706

There is probably a much better way to do this by extracting the
relevant plot sizes from gtable, and then pushing an appropriate
viewport for the plot, but I haven't looked into it myself.

b.

