HI everyone,

this is a direct report from stack overflor: http://stackoverflow.com/questions/9502003/ggplot-scale-y-log10-issue

however I think the issue has reached the point where I think I have exposed a bug (as opposed to me not knowing how to use ggplot). basically the scale becomes wrong when the fill variable is different from the x-variable for ggplot bar graphs. In the following examples, example1 will have the appropriate scale but example 2 will  not:

example_1 = ggplot(diamonds, aes(x=clarity, fill=clarity)) + geom_bar() + scale_y_log10(); print(example_1)
example_2 = ggplot(diamonds, aes(x=clarity, fill=cut)) + geom_bar() + scale_y_log10(); print(example_1)

not sure how to troubleshoot this one but hopefully someone else might,

thanks,
zach cp

